{"timestamp": "2026-08-11T15:34:23.489180+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-39226870-d4a4-4ebc-84ee-a36350dfef12', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': \"You prepare the educational structure of one approved lesson.\\n\\nThe path owns the objective. The skeleton owns section count, order, and purpose.\\nA later planner will choose page blocks. You must not choose components, page\\nobjects, layouts, or question text.\\n\\n## FIXED INPUT\\n\\n- objective and objective_hash\\n- concept_id\\n- primary_knowledge_type\\n- lesson_mode\\n- ordered skeleton slots\\n- scope_contract\\n- prior_established\\n- explicit prerequisites\\n- lesson_actuals\\n- carried anchor, when present\\n- resource identity and purpose\\n\\n## YOUR DECISIONS\\n\\n1. Draft zero to three real misconceptions. Each must support a confident wrong\\n   answer. A missing term is a knowledge gap, not a misconception.\\n2. Reuse the carried anchor when it fits. Otherwise choose one concrete anchor\\n   and state why it is new.\\n3. Give each fixed section a concise title and transition note.\\n4. Preserve section IDs and roles exactly as supplied.\\n5. Attach the canonical concept card ID where required.\\n6. Echo each supplied slot's `visual_required` flag exactly. A true flag is\\n   authoritative and must not be cleared or inferred away.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n- Never change the objective or concept ID.\\n- Never add, remove, reorder, or rename a skeleton slot.\\n- Never choose a component, page object, pedagogical block intent, placement,\\n  or visual form.\\n- Never write question text.\\n- Never reteach prior_established in the structural rationale.\\n- Never introduce must_not_introduce content.\\n- Never manufacture a misconception to fill a count.\\n- Never choose page blocks, intents, objects, or briefs. A later planner\\n  owns the teaching design.\\n\\nIf the objective cannot honestly fit the skeleton, emit deviation_request.\\nIf the objective itself is wrong, emit objective_concern. Do not repair either.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only, matching the supplied output schema.\\n\\nThe output contains:\\n\\n- anchor\\n- one concept card\\n- sections with id, title, role, card_id, visual_required, transition_note\\n- deviation_request or null\\n- objective_concern or null\\n\\nIt contains no components and no blocks.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n1. Is the objective verbatim?\\n2. Do section IDs and order exactly match the fixed slots?\\n3. Does every misconception pass the confident-wrong-answer test?\\n4. Did I choose any page form or teaching block? Remove it.\\n5. Did I contradict prior_established, terminology, or exclusions?\\n\"}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"PathAnchor\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"source\": {\"enum\": [\"carried\", \"new\"], \"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"description\", \"source\"], \"title\": \"PathAnchor\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathDeviationRequest\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"operation\": {\"enum\": [\"insert\", \"remove\", \"replace\", \"reorder\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"target_slot\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"replacement_slot\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}]}, \"reason\": {\"type\": \"string\"}}, \"required\": [\"operation\", \"target_slot\", \"replacement_slot\", \"reason\"], \"title\": \"PathDeviationRequest\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralCard\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Echo concept_id verbatim. The path layer owns this value.\"}, \"title\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Echo the supplied objective verbatim. Never rewrite it.\"}, \"prereqs\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"misconceptions\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralMisconception\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"no_known_misconceptions\": {\"default\": false, \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"opens_by\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralCard\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralComponentSlot\": {\"description\": \"Legacy component-selector shape. Ignored entirely on the native page path.\", \"properties\": {\"slug\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"purpose\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"slug\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralComponentSlot\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralMisconception\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"description\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"The wrong belief, stated the way a learner would state it.\"}, \"statement\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"source\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"title\": \"PathStructuralMisconception\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"PathStructuralSection\": {\"properties\": {\"id\": {\"description\": \"Must equal slots[i].slot_id verbatim, in the supplied order. The field is named \\'id\\' \\\\u2014 do not emit a key called \\'slot_id\\'.\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"role\": {\"description\": \"Must ALSO equal slots[i].slot_id verbatim \\\\u2014 not slots[i].role.\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": {\"description\": \"Concise section title. Aim for ~80 chars (advisory).\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"card_id\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"concept_id for teaching sections; null for plain sections.\"}, \"visual_required\": {\"description\": \"Echo the fixed slot\\'s visual_required flag exactly. A true flag is authoritative and must not be cleared.\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}, \"transition_note\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null, \"description\": \"Why this section follows the previous one. Null for the first section only. Aim for ~120 chars (advisory).\"}, \"components\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralComponentSlot\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"id\", \"role\", \"title\", \"visual_required\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"anchor\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathAnchor\"}, \"cards\": {\"description\": \"Exactly one concept card, unless emitting objective_concern.\", \"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralCard\"}, \"maxItems\": 1, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathStructuralSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}, \"deviation_request\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/PathDeviationRequest\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}, \"objective_concern\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"anchor\"], \"title\": \"PathStructuralPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"component_selections\": {},\\n  \"concept_id\": \"b959d3d6-87cb-48d7-9cb0-c113edbf2e0b\",\\n  \"exclusions\": [],\\n  \"external_prerequisites\": [],\\n  \"group_ids\": [],\\n  \"groups\": [],\\n  \"lesson_actuals\": [],\\n  \"must_establish\": [\\n    \"draw a diagram with arrows showing the flow of water between the Earth\\'s surface and the atmosphere\",\\n    \"label the processes: evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection\",\\n    \"include and label water bodies (e.g., ocean, lake, river) and clouds\",\\n    \"explain the water cycle orally or in writing, using the diagram to trace the movement of water\"\\n  ],\\n  \"native_whole_lesson\": true,\\n  \"objective\": \"Draw a clear labelled diagram of the water cycle showing evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, and the movement of water, and describe the cycle using the diagram\",\\n  \"objective_hash\": \"bbf2d6c51c3f773205837ec89fd4da16434d1a68ba2baf9e6058832c67e95483\",\\n  \"prerequisites\": [\\n    {\\n      \"concept_id\": \"ab4dc26d-787e-4b69-95fe-a871aeb9cab0\",\\n      \"objective\": \"Define evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection and describe how they work together in the water cycle\",\\n      \"path_lesson_id\": \"8f2b71a0-328e-4c84-8ba3-f5d129941fd5\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \"primary_knowledge_type\": \"procedural\",\\n  \"prior_established\": [\\n    \"water exists in different states (solid, liquid, gas)\",\\n    \"water is found in different places such as rivers, lakes, oceans, clouds, and rain\",\\n    \"water can change state when heated or cooled\",\\n    \"define evaporation as the change from liquid water to water vapor caused by heat from the Sun\",\\n    \"define condensation as the change from water vapor to liquid water forming clouds\",\\n    \"define precipitation as water falling from clouds as rain, snow, sleet, or hail\",\\n    \"define collection as the gathering of water in rivers, lakes, and oceans\",\\n    \"explain that the Sun\\'s heat drives evaporation from bodies of water\",\\n    \"describe the sequence: evaporation \\\\u2192 condensation \\\\u2192 precipitation \\\\u2192 collection, linking each process to the next\"\\n  ],\\n  \"scope_contract\": {\\n    \"assumed_prerequisites\": [],\\n    \"may_include\": [],\\n    \"must_establish\": [\\n      \"Define evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection in the context of the water cycle\",\\n      \"Explain how the Sun\\'s energy drives evaporation\",\\n      \"Describe the sequence of processes that move water through the cycle\",\\n      \"Construct a labelled diagram showing the water cycle\"\\n    ],\\n    \"must_not_introduce\": [\\n      \"transpiration\",\\n      \"sublimation\",\\n      \"groundwater flow\",\\n      \"water table\",\\n      \"detailed cloud formation beyond condensation\",\\n      \"atmospheric layers\"\\n    ],\\n    \"notation\": null,\\n    \"terminology\": [\\n      \"evaporation\",\\n      \"condensation\",\\n      \"precipitation\",\\n      \"collection\",\\n      \"water cycle\",\\n      \"water vapor\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \"secondary_demand\": null,\\n  \"slots\": [\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"hook-hero\",\\n        \"interview-anchor\",\\n        \"insight-strip\",\\n        \"timeline-block\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Give the learner a reason to care and a concrete situation to hold.\",\\n      \"role\": \"orient\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"prerequisite-strip\",\\n        \"key-fact\",\\n        \"definition-card\",\\n        \"short-answer\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Reactivate the specific prior knowledge this lesson depends on. Nothing else.\",\\n      \"role\": \"recall\",\\n      \"slot_id\": \"recall\",\\n      \"visual_required\": false\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"allowed_components\": [\\n        \"worked-example-card\",\\n        \"process-steps\",\\n        \"diagram-series\",\\n        \"explanation-block\"\\n      ],\\n      \"locked\": false,\\n      \"purpose\": \"Show the method being carried out, with each step\\'s reason