{"timestamp": "2026-08-11T15:45:13.120734+00:00", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "openai._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'User-Agent': 'pydantic-ai/1.107.1'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-54639339-3258-4da0-8de3-5cfbb09b9581', 'security': {'bearer_auth': True}, 'content': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You choose the physical form of every block in one lesson.\\n\\nThe teaching is already decided and is not yours to change. Each block has a\\njob and a brief. You choose the shape on the page that carries it with the\\nleast machinery, and you choose for the whole lesson at once so the document\\nhas rhythm rather than a run of identical shapes.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE BUILDING\\n\\n  Resource: Lesson (lesson)\\n\\n  A lesson is the default full teaching resource. It introduces a concept,\\n  builds understanding, models the method, gives students guided-to-independent\\n  practice, and closes with a retention check.\\n  \\n  A lesson teaches before it asks students to perform independently. It is not\\n  a worksheet, not a quick reference, and not a quiz. The teacher should be\\n  able to use it as the main classroom arc for first contact with a concept.\\n  \\n  The pedagogical arc is: orient -> build -> model -> practice -> close.\\n  Every section must serve that arc. The planner must not skip the modelling\\n  step, and it must not turn the close into a second teaching section.\\n\\n  Use when:\\n    - First exposure to a new concept\\n    - A full classroom lesson with explicit teaching and practice\\n    - When the teacher wants one coherent teaching arc from hook to check\\n    - When learners need explanation before independent work\\n  Never when:\\n    - The teacher only wants practice questions - use a worksheet or practice set\\n    - The teacher only wants a fast definition or reminder - use a quick explainer\\n    - The session is primarily assessment - use a quiz or exit ticket\\n    - Students already know the concept and only need repetition\\n\\n## WHAT YOU ARE GIVEN\\n\\n  arc               how this lesson moves, from the teaching plan\\n  sections          in order, each with its blocks\\n  per block         id, position, intent, brief\\n  available_objects per intent \u2014 the forms that intent permits, narrowed to\\n                    the forms this resource allows. Each carries:\\n                      holds\\n                      earns_its_place_when\\n                      reject_when\\n                      capacity\\n                      placement\\n\\navailable_objects is closed. An object not shown for an intent is not\\navailable for that block, whatever you may know about it.\\n\\n## THE DEFAULT IS PROSE\\n\\nProse is the cheapest form. It carries almost anything. Every other object\\nmust earn its place against it.\\n\\nRead `earns_its_place_when`. If the brief does not already satisfy it, the\\nobject is out \u2014 even when it appears in available_objects. Then read\\n`reject_when` as the counter-test.\\n\\nThe question is never \"could this be a table?\" It is \"does this brief already\\ncontain what a table needs?\"\\n\\n## WORKED DECISION\\n\\n  block: explain-b1\\n  intent: compare\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants by listing what was held the same \u2014 same\\n          pot, same soil, same water \u2014 and identify light as the only\\n          condition that differed.\"\\n  available_objects: [table, prose, questions]\\n\\n    table\\n      earns_its_place_when: two or more columns of comparable values AND two\\n                            or more rows, with every cell fillable\\n      -> two plants x four conditions. Every cell fillable. Earned.\\n\\n    prose\\n      -> would make the reader hold eight facts in sequence and build the\\n         comparison themselves.\\n\\n    questions\\n      -> the brief says compare, not ask.\\n\\n  -> table\\n\\n  Same intent, different brief:\\n\\n  brief: \"Compare the two plants only on whether they received light.\"\\n\\n    table -> one condition, two rows. reject_when: one column of values.\\n  -> prose\\n\\nThe intent did not change. The brief decided the form.\\n\\n## CAPACITY IS REAL\\n\\n`capacity` states what the printed page holds. It is not a style preference.\\n\\nIf the brief needs more than the object\\'s capacity, the object is wrong.\\n\\n  aside          bodyMaxWords 40. The margin column is 56mm. A point needing\\n                 80 words does not become a small aside; it is prose.\\n  aside          maxPerSection 2. A third aside in one section collides with\\n                 the two already floated.\\n  table          columnsMax 4. A fifth column does not fit the main column\\n                 with a readable header.\\n  list           itemsMin 3. Two bullets is a sentence.\\n  choices        optionsMin 3.\\n\\nNever choose an object expecting the writer to compress. The writer will\\neither overflow or cut something that mattered.\\n\\n## RHYTHM ACROSS THE LESSON\\n\\nYou see the whole lesson. Use that.\\n\\nA section-by-section chooser cannot see this:\\n\\n    ORIENT     figure\\n    EXPLAIN    figure\\n    CONFRONT   figure\\n    CHECK      questions\\n\\nEvery choice locally defensible; the document visually flat. You can see it,\\nso prevent it.\\n\\nGuidance, not arithmetic:\\n\\n  - Avoid the same object three times in a row unless the briefs genuinely\\n    demand it. If they do, say so in `reason`.\\n  - Avoid every section opening with the same form.\\n  - Figures are expensive and slow. Two per lesson is usually plenty, and\\n    they should sit where something is genuinely hard to say in words.\\n  - Do not manufacture variety. Two prose blocks in a row are sometimes\\n    exactly right. A table with nothing to tabulate is worse than a run of\\n    prose.\\n\\nVariety serves reading. It is not a quota.\\n\\n## PLACEMENT\\n\\nOnly `aside` may take the margin. Everything else sits in the main column.\\n\\nChoose margin when the point is genuinely parenthetical: true, useful, and not\\npart of the argument the reader is following. Choose main when the reader\\nneeds it in sequence.\\n\\n## WHAT YOU MAY NOT CHANGE\\n\\n  block id\\n  position\\n  section order\\n  intent\\n  brief\\n  evidence_refs, evidence, departure_reason\\n  source_question_ids\\n\\nYou add a form. You change nothing else. If a brief looks wrong to you, choose\\nthe best form for it anyway and note the concern in `reason`.\\n\\n## PROHIBITIONS\\n\\n  Never choose outside available_objects for that block.\\n  Never choose an object whose earns_its_place_when the brief does not meet.\\n  Never choose an object whose capacity the brief exceeds.\\n  Never choose `heading`. Headings come from section titles.\\n  Never choose `answer-key`. It is produced at document level.\\n  Never add a figure because a section looks plain.\\n  Never give one block two objects, or leave a block without one.\\n\\n## OUTPUT\\n\\nJSON only. No preamble, no code fences.\\n\\n{\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"slot_id\": str,\\n      \"forms\": [\\n        {\\n          \"block_id\": str,\\n          \"object\": str,\\n          \"placement\": \"main\" | \"margin\",\\n          \"reason\": str,\\n          \"escalation\": str | null\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n`reason` \u2014 which `earns_its_place_when` clause this brief satisfies, and how.\\nBe specific to this brief. A reason that would fit any brief is not a reason.\\n\\n`escalation` \u2014 if you did not choose prose, what prose would have lost. Null\\nwhen you chose prose.\\n\\nEvery block in the teaching plan must appear exactly once. No extras.\\n\\n## SELF-CHECK\\n\\n  1. Would prose have worked? If yes, why did I not use it?\\n  2. Does the brief actually contain what this object needs, or am I assuming\\n     the writer will produce it?\\n  3. Does the brief fit inside capacity? Count, do not estimate.\\n  4. Read my form choices top to bottom. Does the lesson have rhythm, or is\\n     it three of one thing?\\n  5. Did I add variety that no brief asked for?\\n  6. Does every block from the teaching plan appear exactly once?\\n  7. Is any `reason` generic enough to fit a different block?\\n'}, {'role': 'system', 'content': 'Return only valid JSON matching this schema.\\nDo not call tools.\\n{\"$defs\": {\"FormDecision\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"description\": \"Form-planner owned fields for one teaching block.\", \"properties\": {\"block_id\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"object\": {\"minLength\": 1, \"type\": \"string\"}, \"placement\": {\"default\": \"main\", \"enum\": [\"main\", \"margin\"], \"type\": \"string\"}, \"reason\": {\"default\": \"\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"escalation\": {\"anyOf\": [{\"type\": \"string\"}, {\"type\": \"null\"}], \"default\": null}}, \"required\": [\"block_id\", \"object\"], \"title\": \"FormDecision\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"FormPlanSection\": {\"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"slot_id\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"forms\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormDecision\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"required\": [\"slot_id\"], \"title\": \"FormPlanSection\", \"type\": \"object\"}}, \"additionalProperties\": false, \"properties\": {\"sections\": {\"items\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/FormPlanSection\"}, \"type\": \"array\"}}, \"title\": \"FormPlan\", \"type\": \"object\"}'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{\\n  \"arc\": \"The lesson opens on a disappearing puddle that sparks curiosity about where water goes and how it returns. Students recall the meanings of evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and collection. The teacher models building a labelled diagram of the water cycle, emphasizing the circular flow and the distinction between water vapor and clouds. Guided practice has learners complete and describe their own diagrams, and the lesson closes with a multiple-choice check that diagnoses whether learners still think clouds are water vapor.\",\\n  \"available_objects\": {\\n    \"by_intent\": {\\n      \"activate-prior-knowledge\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"answer-key\": [],\\n      \"apply\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"check-understanding\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"classify\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"compare\": [\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-back\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"connect-forward\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"define\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"demonstrate\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"derive\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"diagnose-misconception\": [\\n        \"choices\",\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"aside\"\\n      ],\\n      \"emphasise\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"evaluate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"explain-cause\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"interpret\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"investigate\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"memory-aid\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"model-thinking\": [\\n        \"worked-example\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"name-parts\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\"\\n      ],\\n      \"orient\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-guided\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"practise-independent\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"choices\"\\n      ],\\n      \"reflect\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"sequence\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"questions\"\\n      ],\\n      \"show-structure\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"state-goal\": [\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"list\"\\n      ],\\n      \"summarise\": [\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"prose\",\\n        \"table\"\\n      ],\\n      \"trace-flow\": [\\n        \"figure\",\\n        \"list\",\\n        \"table\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ],\\n      \"transfer\": [\\n        \"questions\",\\n        \"worked-example\"\\n      ],\\n      \"warn\": [\\n        \"aside\",\\n        \"prose\"\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    \"catalogue_version\": \"1.1.0\",\\n    \"objects\": [\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"bodyMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"labelMaxWords\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"maxPerSection\\\\\": 2}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"memory-aid\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"One short point that must sit outside the reading line without breaking it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"aside\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Longer than the margin column holds, or the point belongs in the flow. If it will not fit in 40 words it is prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'margin\\', \\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"optionMaxWords\\\\\": 15, \\\\\"optionsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"optionsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Selection is the response AND every wrong option carries diagnostic meaning.\",\\n        \"id\": \"choices\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Distractors are filler, or the answer cannot be reduced to a selectable option.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"altTextMaxWords\\\\\": 40, \\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 30}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Spatial, sequential, or structural content the reader would otherwise have to construct mentally.\",\\n        \"id\": \"figure\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Decorative, or the caption would restate the surrounding prose.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"leadInMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"wordsPerItem\\\\\": 25}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"memory-aid\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"investigate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Three or more genuinely parallel items that lose nothing when the connective prose between them is removed.\",\\n        \"id\": \"list\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fewer than three items, or items that need explaining to one another. Two bullets is a sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'margin\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"paragraphsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"paragraphsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"wordsPerParagraph\\\\\": 120}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"orient\",\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"state-goal\",\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"warn\",\\n          \"emphasise\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"connect-forward\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Default. Use unless another object earns its place against it.\",\\n        \"id\": \"prose\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Never rejected. Prose is the fallback.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"itemsMax\\\\\": 6, \\\\\"itemsMin\\\\\": 1, \\\\\"stemMaxWords\\\\\": 45}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"practise-independent\",\\n          \"check-understanding\",\\n          \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"connect-back\",\\n          \"reflect\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"The learner must produce something in their own words or working.\",\\n        \"id\": \"questions\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"Fixed options exist \\\\u2014 use choices. Or nothing is actually being asked.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"captionMaxWords\\\\\": 20, \\\\\"columnsMax\\\\\": 4, \\\\\"columnsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"rowsMax\\\\\": 8, \\\\\"rowsMin\\\\\": 2, \\\\\"wordsPerCell\\\\\": 12}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"define\",\\n          \"name-parts\",\\n          \"classify\",\\n          \"compare\",\\n          \"sequence\",\\n          \"explain\",\\n          \"explain-cause\",\\n          \"trace-flow\",\\n          \"show-structure\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"interpret\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"summarise\",\\n          \"investigate\",\\n          \"evaluate\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"Two or more columns of comparable values AND two or more rows, with every cell fillable.\",\\n        \"id\": \"table\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"One column of values, or any cell that would be empty, \\'n/a\\', or a full sentence.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      },\\n      {\\n        \"capacity_summary\": \"{\\\\\"problemMaxWords\\\\\": 60, \\\\\"stepsMax\\\\\": 7, \\\\\"stepsMin\\\\\": 3, \\\\\"wordsPerStep\\\\\": 40}\",\\n        \"choose_when\": \"\",\\n        \"compatible_intents\": [\\n          \"demonstrate\",\\n          \"model-thinking\",\\n          \"derive\",\\n          \"apply\",\\n          \"transfer\",\\n          \"practise-guided\"\\n        ],\\n        \"earns_its_place_when\": \"A complete instance from setup to answer, with every step visible.\",\\n        \"id\": \"worked-example\",\\n        \"not_when\": \"No final answer, or steps the learner is meant to supply themselves.\",\\n        \"placement_restrictions\": \"[\\'main\\', \\'spanning\\']\"\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \"projection_hash\": \"05fddc80790c232176df5c03bf7ea1ead8b910d06c848b4836be205a7552c98b\"\\n  },\\n  \"lesson\": {\\n    \"grade_level\": \"Grade 6\",\\n    \"objective\": \"Draw a clear labelled diagram of the water cycle showing evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection, and the movement of water, and describe the cycle using the diagram\",\\n    \"subject\": \"Science\"\\n  },\\n  \"required_visual_slots\": [\\n    \"model\"\\n  ],\\n  \"sections\": [\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Present the anchor: a puddle on a playground after rain that slowly disappears over sunny days, then reappears after the next rain. Ask, \\'Where does the water go, and how does it return?\\' Do not explain the water cycle yet; only establish the phenomenon and the question.\",\\n          \"id\": \"orient-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"orient\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"orient\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Prompt students to recall the definitions of evaporation (liquid to water vapor driven by Sun\\'s heat), condensation (water vapor to liquid forming clouds), precipitation (water falling as rain, snow, etc.), and collection (water gathering in rivers, lakes, oceans). Also have them state the sequence: evaporation \\\\u2192 condensation \\\\u2192 precipitation \\\\u2192 collection. Use quick verbal responses.\",\\n          \"id\": \"recall-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"activate-prior-knowledge\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"prose\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"recall\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Draw a diagram step by step: (1) Place a large body of water at the bottom, label \\'Collection (ocean/lake)\\'. (2) Add the sun above, write \\'Sun\\\\u2019s energy\\'. (3) Draw an upward arrow from the water to the sky, label \\'Evaporation (water vapor)\\'. Explicitly note that water vapor is an invisible gas, so the arrow represents the vapor. (4) Draw cloud shapes at the top, label \\'Condensation (clouds)\\' and clarify that clouds are tiny liquid water droplets, not gas. (5) Draw a downward arrow from clouds to land and water, label \\'Precipitation (rain, etc.)\\'. (6) Add an arrow from land back to the ocean, label \\'Collection\\'. This block fulfills the visual requirement by showing labels and spatial arrangement.\",\\n          \"id\": \"model-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"show-structure\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Using the completed diagram, trace the flow: \\'The Sun\\'s energy causes evaporation from the ocean; water vapor rises and condenses into clouds (condensation); clouds release precipitation; water collects in the ocean again. The cycle repeats continuously \\\\u2014 it is not one-way.\\' Connect back to the puddle: puddle water evaporates, condenses into clouds, falls as rain, and re-fills the puddle. Emphasize the circular nature to pre-empt M2.\",\\n          \"id\": \"model-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"sequence\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"figure\",\\n            \"list\",\\n            \"table\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"model\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Provide a partially drawn diagram showing an ocean, sun, and cloud outlines, but missing the four process labels and arrows. Guide students to add the labels (evaporation, condensation, precipitation, collection) and draw the arrows showing water movement. Offer prompts: \\'What happens when the sun heats the water? Where does the water go after it evaporates? What are clouds made of?\\' Explicitly address M1: remind them that water vapor is an invisible gas, so clouds are not water vapor \\\\u2014 they are condensation (liquid water droplets). Walk around and give corrective feedback.\",\\n          \"id\": \"guided-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"worked-example\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Ask students to turn to a partner and, using their completed diagram, describe the full water cycle, naming each process in order. Give sentence starters: \\'The Sun\\'s energy causes...\\', \\'When water vapor rises...\\', \\'After rain falls...\\'. Circulate and prompt for missing steps. This builds fluency in describing the cycle, addressing the second part of the objective.\",\\n          \"id\": \"guided-b2\",\\n          \"intent\": \"practise-guided\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"worked-example\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 1\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"guided\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \"blocks\": [\\n        {\\n          \"brief\": \"Administer a multiple-choice question that tests whether the learner correctly identifies that water vapor is an invisible gas and clouds are liquid water droplets. The item must have at least one distractor that labels clouds as water vapor (gas). Do not add new teaching; use only the approved item.\",\\n          \"id\": \"check-b1\",\\n          \"intent\": \"diagnose-misconception\",\\n          \"legal_object_candidates\": [\\n            \"choices\"\\n          ],\\n          \"position\": 0\\n        }\\n      ],\\n      \"slot_id\": \"check\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}'}], 'model': 'deepseek-v4-flash', 'max_completion_tokens': 120000, 'stream': False}}"}
